{"id":"mahabharata-3-028","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":28,"title":"अष्टाविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 28 · Draupadi's reproach","summary":{"en":"One evening Draupadi reproaches Yudhishthira: seeing his brothers and herself suffering in the forest, how can his anger not rise against those who wronged them? A kshatriya who never shows anger, she says, is despised by all.","kn":"ಒಂದು ಸಂಜೆ ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನನ್ನು ಆಕ್ಷೇಪಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ: ಸಹೋದರರೂ ತಾನೂ ಕಾಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ನರಳುತ್ತಿರುವುದನ್ನು ಕಂಡೂ ಅನ್ಯಾಯ ಮಾಡಿದವರ ಮೇಲೆ ನಿನ್ನ ಕೋಪ ಏಕೆ ಏಳದು? ಎಂದೂ ಕೋಪ ತೋರದ ಕ್ಷತ್ರಿಯನನ್ನು ಎಲ್ಲರೂ ತಿರಸ್ಕರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"एक सन्ध्या द्रौपदी युधिष्ठिर को उलाहना देती हैं: भाइयों और उन्हें वन में कष्ट सहते देखकर भी अन्याय करने वालों पर उनका क्रोध क्यों नहीं उठता? वे कहती हैं कि जो क्षत्रिय कभी क्रोध नहीं दिखाता, उसका सब तिरस्कार करते हैं।","te":"ఒక సాయంత్రం ద్రౌపది యుధిష్ఠిరుని నిందిస్తుంది: సోదరులు, తాను అడవిలో కష్టపడుతుండడం చూసి కూడా అన్యాయం చేసినవారిపై నీ కోపం ఎందుకు లేవదు? ఎన్నడూ కోపం చూపని క్షత్రియుని అందరూ తిరస్కరిస్తారంటుంది.","ta":"ஒரு மாலை திரௌபதி யுதிஷ்டிரரைக் கடிகிறாள்: சகோதரர்களும் தானும் காட்டில் துன்புறுவதைக் கண்டும் அநீதி செய்தவர்கள் மீது உம் சினம் ஏன் எழவில்லை? ஒருபோதும் சினம் காட்டாத க்ஷத்ரியனை அனைவரும் இகழ்வார்கள் என்கிறாள்.","ml":"ഒരു സായാഹ്നത്തിൽ ദ്രൗപദി യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ ശാസിക്കുന്നു: കാട്ടിൽ സഹോദരന്മാരും താനും കഷ്ടപ്പെടുന്നത് കാണുമ്പോൾ, തങ്ങളോട് തെറ്റുചെയ്തവരോട് അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് കോപം ഉണരാത്തതെങ്ങനെ? ഒരിക്കലും കോപം കാണിക്കാത്ത ക്ഷത്രിയനെ എല്ലാവരും നിന്ദിക്കുമെന്ന് അവൾ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.28; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"कैरातपर्व","titleEn":"Kairata Parva (The mountain hunter)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो वनगताः पार्थाः सायाह्ने सह कृष्णया ।\nउपविष्टाः कथाश्चक्रुर्दुःखशोकपरायणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Parthas, living in the forest, sat down with Krishna one evening and talked, given over to sorrow and grief."}},{"n":2,"text":"प्रिया च दर्शनीया च पण्डिता च पतिव्रता ।\nततः कृष्णा धर्मराजमिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear to them, beautiful, learned and devoted to her husbands, Draupadi then spoke these words to the king of dharma."}},{"n":3,"text":"न नूनं तस्य पापस्य दुःखमस्मासु किंचन ।\nविद्यते धार्तराष्ट्रस्य नृशंसस्य दुरात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely that sinful, cruel and evil-souled son of Dhritarashtra feels no pain at all on our account.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"यस्त्वां राजन्मया सार्धमजिनैः प्रतिवासितम् ।\nभ्रातृभिश्च तथा सर्वैर्नाभ्यभाषत किंचन ।\nवनं प्रस्थाप्य दुष्टात्मा नान्वतप्यत दुर्मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"O king, when you were made to dwell in deerskins with me and all your brothers, he said not a word to you; the wicked fool sent you to the forest and felt no remorse.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"आयसं हृदयं नूनं तस्य दुष्कृतकर्मणः ।\nयस्त्वां धर्मपरं श्रेष्ठं रूक्षाण्यश्रावयत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely the heart of that evildoer is made of iron, for he spoke harsh words then to you, the best man, devoted to dharma.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"सुखोचितमदुःखार्हं दुरात्मा ससुहृद्गणः ।\nईदृशं दुःखमानीय मोदते पापपूरुषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That evil man with his band of friends, having brought on us a sorrow so unfit for people used to comfort, rejoices, the sinner.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"चतुर्णामेव पापानामश्रु वै नापतत्तदा ।\nत्वयि भारत निष्क्रान्ते वनायाजिनवाससि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Only four sinners shed no tear when you, Bharata, set out for the forest in deerskins.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"दुर्योधनस्य कर्णस्य शकुनेश्च दुरात्मनः ।\nदुर्भ्रातुस्तस्य चोग्रस्य तथा दुःशासनस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They were Duryodhana, Karna, the evil Shakuni, and the fierce, ill-natured brother Duhshasana.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"इतरेषां तु सर्वेषां कुरूणां कुरुसत्तम ।\nदुःखेनाभिपरीतानां नेत्रेभ्यः प्रापतज्जलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But all the other Kurus, best of the Kurus, overcome with grief, had tears streaming from their eyes.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"इदं च शयनं दृष्ट्वा यच्चासीत्ते पुरातनम् ।\nशोचामि त्वां महाराज दुःखानर्हं सुखोचितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing this bed, and recalling your old one, great king, I grieve for you, who deserve no sorrow and are used to comfort.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"दान्तं यच्च सभामध्ये आसनं रत्नभूषितम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा कुशबृसीं चेमां शोको मां रुन्धयत्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing the jeweled seat you had in the assembly and now this mat of kusha grass, grief chokes me.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"यदपश्यं सभायां त्वां राजभिः परिवारितम् ।\nतच्च राजन्नपश्यन्त्याः का शान्तिर्हृदयस्य मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When I saw you in the hall surrounded by kings, and now cannot see that, O king, what peace can there be for my heart?\""}},{"n":13,"text":"या त्वाहं चन्दनादिग्धमपश्यं सूर्यवर्चसम् ।\nसा त्वा पङ्कमलादिग्धं दृष्ट्वा मुह्यामि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I saw you smeared with sandal paste, shining like the sun; seeing you now covered with mud and dirt, Bharata, I am bewildered.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"या वै त्वा कौशिकैर्वस्त्रैः शुभ्रैर्बहुधनैः पुरा ।\nदृष्टवत्यस्मि राजेन्द्र सा त्वां पश्यामि चीरिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Once I saw you, great king, in fine white silken clothes of great price; now I see you in bark.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"यच्च तद्रुक्मपात्रीभिर्ब्राह्मणेभ्यः सहस्रशः ।\nह्रियते ते गृहादन्नं संस्कृतं सार्वकामिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"From your house food, cooked with every delicacy, used to be carried in golden dishes to brahmins by the thousand.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"यतीनामगृहाणां ते तथैव गृहमेधिनाम् ।\nदीयते भोजनं राजन्नतीव गुणवत्प्रभो ।\nतच्च राजन्नपश्यन्त्याः का शान्तिर्हृदयस्य मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Food of the best quality was given, my lord, to the ascetics who had no home and to householders alike; not seeing that now, what peace can there be for my heart?\""}},{"n":17,"text":"यांस्ते भ्रातॄन्महाराज युवानो मृष्टकुण्डलाः ।\nअभोजयन्त मृष्टान्नैः सूदाः परमसंस्कृतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The young cooks with polished earrings used to feed your brothers, great king, with refined dishes of the finest preparation.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"सर्वांस्तानद्य पश्यामि वने वन्येन जीवतः ।\nअदुःखार्हान्मनुष्येन्द्र नोपशाम्यति मे मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"All of them I now see living in the forest on wild fare, though they do not deserve such hardship, lord of men; my mind finds no rest.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"भीमसेनमिमं चापि दुःखितं वनवासिनम् ।\nध्यायन्तं किं न मन्युस्ते प्राप्ते काले विवर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Why does your anger not grow, now that the time has come, when you see Bhimasena in the forest, suffering and brooding?\""}},{"n":20,"text":"भीमसेनं हि कर्माणि स्वयं कुर्वाणमच्युत ।\nसुखार्हं दुःखितं दृष्ट्वा कस्मान्मन्युर्न वर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Why does your anger not grow, unshaken one, seeing Bhimasena, deserving comfort, doing his tasks himself in misery?\""}},{"n":21,"text":"सत्कृतं विविधैर्यानैर्वस्त्रैरुच्चावचैस्तथा ।\nतं ते वनगतं दृष्ट्वा कस्मान्मन्युर्न वर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Why does your anger not grow, seeing him in the forest, he who was honored with many kinds of vehicles and fine and plain garments?\""}},{"n":22,"text":"कुरूनपि हि यः सर्वान्हन्तुमुत्सहते प्रभुः ।\nत्वत्प्रसादं प्रतीक्षंस्तु सहतेऽयं वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This Vrikodara, who is able to kill all the Kurus, endures it only because he waits for your favor.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"योऽर्जुनेनार्जुनस्तुल्यो द्विबाहुर्बहुबाहुना ।\nशरातिसर्गे शीघ्रत्वात्कालान्तकयमोपमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He is Arjuna's equal, a two-armed man matching the many-armed Arjuna of the Haihayas, and in swiftness of loosing arrows like Death, the destroyer of time and Yama.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"यस्य शस्त्रप्रतापेन प्रणताः सर्वपार्थिवाः ।\nयज्ञे तव महाराज ब्राह्मणानुपतस्थिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By the might of his weapons all the kings bowed and waited on the brahmins at your sacrifice, great king.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"तमिमं पुरुषव्याघ्रं पूजितं देवदानवैः ।\nध्यायन्तमर्जुनं दृष्ट्वा कस्मान्मन्युर्न वर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Why does your anger not grow, seeing this tiger among men, honored by gods and demons, now sitting brooding, Arjuna?\""}},{"n":26,"text":"दृष्ट्वा वनगतं पार्थमदुःखार्हं सुखोचितम् ।\nन च ते वर्धते मन्युस्तेन मुह्यामि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing Partha, who deserves no pain and is used to comfort, living in the forest, your anger does not grow, and that bewilders me, Bharata.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"यो देवांश्च मनुष्यांश्च सर्पांश्चैकरथोऽजयत् ।\nतं ते वनगतं दृष्ट्वा कस्मान्मन्युर्न वर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He conquered gods, men and serpents from a single chariot; why does your anger not grow when you see him in the forest?\""}},{"n":28,"text":"यो यानैरद्भुताकारैर्हयैर्नागैश्च संवृतः ।\nप्रसह्य वित्तान्यादत्त पार्थिवेभ्यः परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surrounded by wonderful chariots, horses and elephants, that scorcher of foes forcibly took the wealth of kings.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"क्षिपत्येकेन वेगेन पञ्च बाणशतानि यः ।\nतं ते वनगतं दृष्ट्वा कस्मान्मन्युर्न वर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He shoots five hundred arrows in a single burst; why does your anger not grow when you see him in the forest?\""}},{"n":30,"text":"श्यामं बृहन्तं तरुणं चर्मिणामुत्तमं रणे ।\nनकुलं ते वने दृष्ट्वा कस्मान्मन्युर्न वर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Why does your anger not grow when you see in the forest Nakula, dark, tall, young, the best of shield-bearers in battle?\""}},{"n":31,"text":"दर्शनीयं च शूरं च माद्रीपुत्रं युधिष्ठिर ।\nसहदेवं वने दृष्ट्वा कस्मान्मन्युर्न वर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Why does your anger not grow, Yudhishthira, when you see Sahadeva, the handsome and heroic son of Madri, in the forest?\""}},{"n":32,"text":"द्रुपदस्य कुले जातां स्नुषां पाण्डोर्महात्मनः ।\nमां ते वनगतां दृष्ट्वा कस्मान्मन्युर्न वर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Why does your anger not grow when you see me, born in Drupada's family and daughter-in-law of the great Pandu, living in the forest?\""}},{"n":33,"text":"नूनं च तव नैवास्ति मन्युर्भरतसत्तम ।\nयत्ते भ्रातॄंश्च मां चैव दृष्ट्वा न व्यथते मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely you have no anger at all, best of the Bharatas, since your mind does not ache at the sight of your brothers and me.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"न निर्मन्युः क्षत्रियोऽस्ति लोके निर्वचनं स्मृतम् ।\nतदद्य त्वयि पश्यामि क्षत्रिये विपरीतवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"It is said that there is no warrior in the world without anger; yet today I see in you, a warrior, the opposite.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"यो न दर्शयते तेजः क्षत्रियः काल आगते ।\nसर्वभूतानि तं पार्थ सदा परिभवन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A warrior who does not show his fire when the time comes is always scorned by all beings, Partha.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"तत्त्वया न क्षमा कार्या शत्रून्प्रति कथंचन ।\nतेजसैव हि ते शक्या निहन्तुं नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So you should not show patience toward your enemies in any way; by fire alone can you surely kill them.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"तथैव यः क्षमाकाले क्षत्रियो नोपशाम्यति ।\nअप्रियः सर्वभूतानां सोऽमुत्रेह च नश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Likewise a warrior who does not calm down when it is the time for forbearance becomes hateful to all beings and is ruined both here and hereafter.\""}}]}]}